# KineticWE ships every Spectacle action unbound. Spectacle (a regular KDE
# app, not part of KineticWE) registers its defaults with the embedded
# kglobalaccel daemon: the "Start/Stop Screen Recording" shortcut (desktop
# action id `RecordScreen`) defaults to Meta+Alt+R, which is the same chord
# the compositor gives to NoctaliaRestartShell — the daemon drops the chord
# on conflict, so neither action fires. The screenshot actions default to
# Print-family chords and the launcher to Print/Meta+Shift+S, which we also
# clear so KineticWE never overrides a user's preferred shortcuts. Making
# every Spectacle bind empty by default keeps the install conflict-free;
# users who want Spectacle's shortcuts can rebind them in Kinetic Settings →
# Keybinds → Spectacle.
#
# Action ids below come from /usr/share/kglobalaccel/org.kde.spectacle.desktop
# (`[Desktop Action ...]` headers), NOT from the localized `Name=...` strings.
# `_launch` is the "Spectacle" launcher action.
[org.kde.spectacle.desktop][Global Shortcuts]
_launch=
FullScreenScreenShot=
CurrentMonitorScreenShot=
ActiveWindowScreenShot=
RectangularRegionScreenShot=
WindowUnderCursorScreenShot=
OpenWithoutScreenshot=
RecordRegion=
RecordScreen=
RecordWindow=

